{"id": "idaho-1", "headline": "Idaho ranks first for foster homes per child", "source": "Idaho Capital Sun", "url": "https://idahocapitalsun.com/2026/11/24/federal-official-highlights-idahos-success-in-increasing-foster-home-to-child-ratio/", "published": "2026-11-24", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["Alex Adams, a federal Administration for Children and Families assistant secretary and Idaho's former state health director, visited Boise on Monday to highlight the state's gains in foster care. A new federal child welfare scorecard ranks states on measures including the ratio of foster homes to foster children and family placement. Adams said Idaho is in the pole position. He announced a federal competition among states to encourage healthy competition. Idaho ranks first in the nation for the ratio, though some counties still lack enough foster homes. Adams met with state, local and nonprofit officials to discuss the changes. Source: Idaho Capital Sun."], "qr": {"n": 41, "rows": ["11111110011010001011100111100111101111111", "10000010100000011000111010111010001000001", "10111010011100110011111000101000101011101", "10111010101010000111001011100100001011101", "10111010010000111011100100000011101011101", "10000010100011100100001001011010101000001", "11111110101010101010101010101010101111111", "00000000001010101010111100001000100000000", "11111011101111100101001101010101110101010", "01000100100111001111110110100111111111011", "00110010011111110000111011111100110010000", "01001100000001010000111110011010001111000", "00000111101100100101000011100101000001110", "11110000000011010001110100001111011110101", "00000011000000010100101010010000010100000", "01101000100010010010010010001011100011010", "01011110111011110101001101000101000000100", "01001100010110001011000111101001111110011", "10000011101000011110011001111110000110000", "01111000000110111010111100101000000001010", "10000111101010000101001111100100000001100", "10001000010001110111111100101001101111101", "010101100011101